WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:06.570
This is a working twin of a container terminal, built for the PS18 program.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.870
Three things have to be proven here.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.370
First, positioning.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.570
Watch the two confidence bars as the vehicle enters the container canyon.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:19.570
Satellite positioning degrades under the quay cranes, and the fusion estimate holds.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.570
7 cm in the open, 22 cm under the crane.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.070
Second, navigation.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:30.570
Congestion aware routing between the stacks, with obstacle safe stops in mixed traffic.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.570
Third, scheduling.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.070
The dispatch toggle switches between first in, first out, and predictive arrival time,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.570
and crane idle moves in response, the number a terminal operator is paid on.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.070
Note the badge. Shadow mode.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.070
It advises before it is given control, which is how a port adopts this.
